      "writtenOn": "2025-09-15T19:50:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please use `SkASSERT_RELEASE` instead of `SkASSERT`.  I believe this is what is recommended by the guidance at https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/styleguide/c++/checks.md#invariant_verification-mechanisms: \"Prefer CHECK() and NOTREACHED() over DCHECK()\".  FWIW I think that using `SkASSERT_RELEASE` has been quite beneficial for launching Rust PNG, because it meant that most fuzzer-discovered bugs did not have any security impact (only stability impact).\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n    SkASSERT_RELEASE(fullImageBuffer.size() \u003e\u003d dst.size());\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 641,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 641,
